{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For he is going.</b> He saw that the matter was evil in the eyes of the Omnipresent, and he longed to go." "<b>For an adversary to him.</b> He was an angel of mercy, and he wanted to prevent him from sinning — so that he would not sin and perish." "<b>And his two lads with him.</b> From here: a prominent man who sets out on the road takes two men with him to attend him, and they take turns and attend each other."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:13.209567096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}